index 4479b53..6a69fa8 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,37 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Account settings and passkey service
+
+Account settings are available at `/devtools-times/account/settings` after password sign-in.
+The app exchanges the existing account service's login token for a one-hour, server-side
+Astro session; the upstream token is never sent to browser JavaScript. The Node adapter
+uses filesystem session storage by default. Multi-instance deployments need a shared
+Astro session driver.
+
+Set `ACCOUNT_API_URL` at build time to override the existing account API base URL.
+This repository contains the settings UI and authenticated API adapter, **not** the
+external account service or its credential database. That service must implement:
+
+| Endpoint | Contract |
+| --- | --- |
+| `POST /login` | Accept `{ username, password }`; return `{ token }` on successful authentication. |
+| `GET /credentials` | Authenticate the bearer token; return the signed-in user's **complete** credential list as `{ rpId, userId, credentials }`. |
+| `PUT /credential/:id` | Authenticate the bearer token, enforce credential ownership, and persist `{ name }` (1–80 trimmed characters). |
+| `DELETE /credential/:id` | Authenticate the bearer token, enforce credential ownership, and permanently revoke the credential. |
+
+Each credential has `{ id, name, aaguid?, registeredAt, lastUsedAt? }`. Dates are epoch
+milliseconds; IDs and `userId` must be genuine unpadded Base64URL values. `rpId` must
+match the value used for registration. The list must not be paginated: browser sync
+treats omitted IDs as revoked. Never return another user's credentials. Ownership
+must also be checked by the external service atomically when applying each mutation.
+No credential seed data or local mock authentication is used. If these external
+endpoints are unavailable, the UI displays a retryable error.
+
+The browser signals the complete accepted credential list on page load and after
+successful deletion. Unsupported browsers and sync failures retain working account
+management and show instructions to update the password manager manually. Individual
+passkey nicknames are account labels; they do not change WebAuthn user details.
+Provider hints use a bundled subset of the [community AAGUID registry](https://github.com/passkeydeveloper/passkey-authenticator-aaguids),
+with a generic fallback for unknown or zero AAGUIDs. These hints never affect authorization.
